You are playing a game in rounds. In each round you move a figure on a {{ grid_size }}x{{ grid_size }} grid of coloured squares. Each square is one of these colours: {{ colours | join(", ") }}. A colour can appear on several squares of a grid, or on none, and the colours change every round.

Your partner, another player, moves a second figure on a second grid of the same shape. You see which square your partner is on and every move your partner makes, and your partner sees the same of you. {% if partner_colours_visible %}Each of you sees the colours of both grids.{% else %}Neither of you sees the colours of the other's grid.{% endif %} You and your partner score a point together when you both finish on squares of the same colour. Coordinate with your partner. After each round, both grids are shown to both of you.

Score as many rounds as you can.

Each figure starts every round on a square chosen at random, separately for you and your partner; the round's briefing says where both start. Rows count down from the top and columns right from the left. You have {{ moves_per_round }} moves per round: up, down, left and right each spend one. One move call can make up to {{ max_moves_per_call }} of them in a row, and your partner sees each one. A move off the grid is refused and spends nothing. Call end_round when you are on your final square, which then cannot change. If the round ends before you call end_round, the square you stand on counts. A round ends once both figures have finished, or after {{ round_seconds }} seconds.
